cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. If you use the scroll data, also cite the Vesuvius Challenge
  dataset as described in DATA_NOTICE.md.
title: "hercules: controlled, falsifiable ink reads for Herculaneum scroll segments"
abstract: >-
  Quality control for ink-detection reads on Vesuvius Challenge segments. The tools pair every forward read with its
  depth-reversed read as a matched negative control, refuse truncated prediction maps, mask by CT, tile a frozen
  pre-registered unit rule, fire a tripwire on mirrored surfaces, and compute the layout-aware probability that a
  surface could produce a candidate at all. Included: a known-text control on a training-set sheet of the ink model,
  re-created byte for byte in a fresh container; a pre-registered held-out known-text test on an unseen scroll
  (PHerc0841: pixel AUC 0.8393 forward, 0.5486 reverse; the frozen unit screen flags 1 of 60 units); and 37
  documented lessons.
type: software
